$ ./toytool --help
toytool - Toy tool for spike D

Usage:
  toytool COMMAND
  toytool [COMMAND] --help | -h
  toytool --version | -v

Commands:
  show          Read a JSON file and print a table
  delete        Delete a file
  completions   Generate bash completion script

Options:
  --help, -h
    Show this help

  --version, -v
    Show version number


$ ./toytool show --help
toytool show - Read a JSON file and print a table

Usage:
  toytool show FILE [OPTIONS]
  toytool show --help | -h

Options:
  --output FORMAT
    Output format
    Allowed: table, json, csv, tsv
    Default: table

  --help, -h
    Show this help

Arguments:
  FILE
    JSON file to read

Examples:
  toytool show data.json

